    {
      "id": "claim_b1f04e71ff654af1aecc2ceb9e6b02b1",
      "statement": "If the per-wiki workspace is lost, the database row survives but the log and wiki.zip are gone; a git source is recoverable because POST /wikis/{id}/retry re-claims the wiki and _fetch re-clones using the token still stored in the source JSON column, whereas an uploaded archive is unrecoverable because the archive itself lived in the job directory and the pipeline raises \"the uploaded archive is no longer available; submit the wiki again\".",
